## AC "3 (colour part)" — full sequence, both viewports
Script: /tmp/claude-1000/th1-checker-a11y/seq-test.js
Sequence per viewport: load -> click [data-ins-tab="income"] -> click
[data-ins-tab="trends"] -> real click #theme-toggle -> click
[data-trends-toggle] ("Show all") -> real click #theme-toggle again.
Read chart.data[0]/[1].marker.color, chart.layout.height,
#chart-trends.getBoundingClientRect().height, and visible tbody row count,
after every step.

Results (1300 and 390 identical):
  initial-load-light:            trace0 rgb(79,70,229)   trace1 #78716c   height 576  rows 12  bars 12
  after-tab-away-and-back-light: trace0 rgb(79,70,229)   trace1 #78716c   height 576  rows 12  bars 12
  after-theme-toggle-dark:       trace0 rgb(165,180,252) trace1 #a8a29e   height 576  rows 12  bars 12
  after-show-all-toggle-dark:    trace0 rgb(165,180,252) trace1 #a8a29e   height 1678 rows 41  bars 41
  after-second-theme-toggle-light: trace0 rgb(79,70,229) trace1 #78716c   height 1678 rows 41  bars 41

Every trace colour matches the brief's expected values exactly in every
step, including the load->tab-away->tab-back->theme-toggle sequence the
brief called out as the regression path (the prior Plotly.restyle-only
implementation was fixed by TC1/attempt2 for colour but the TH1 defect was
specifically about height surviving a tab-switch-then-theme-toggle, tested
below). Category labels confirmed present in chart.data[0].y (12 and 41
entries, human-readable category names, e.g. "Lucid payment",
"Health insurance", ... "Ignore"). chart.data[0].x holds the numeric
amounts (Plotly swaps x/y for horizontal bars per charts.js:182-189, as the
brief noted). Height math verified: 12*38+120=576, 41*38+120=1678, matching
filterTrendTraces's Math.max(360, categories.length*38+120). No console
errors in either viewport (consoleErrors: [] both).

