## AC "height must not collapse on tab-switch-then-theme-toggle" (the TH1 defect)
This is the specific regression the code comment documents: activating
another Insights tab used to call Plotly.Plots.resize() on #chart-trends,
which (with no explicit layout.height pinned) reset height to Plotly's
default, collapsing the container to the page's 300px CSS min-height —
invisible until the NEXT themechange (which only restyled marker, never
height). The seq-test above exercises exactly that path (tab away, tab
back, THEN toggle theme) and shows layout.height and the rendered
getBoundingClientRect height both staying at 576 (12 rows) / 1678 (41 rows)
through every step — never dropping to 300. Confirmed fixed.

## AC "text alternative stays in step with chart" (point 11)
In every one of the 5 sequence steps above, the visible tbody row count
equals chart.data[0].y.length exactly (12=12, 41=41) — table and chart
never diverge in any state, including immediately after a theme toggle.

