## Keyboard (point 9)
Script: /tmp/claude-1000/th1-checker-a11y/keyboard-test2.js and
tab-walk.js. Arrow-key roving tabindex on the Insights tablist still works
after the change (ArrowRight trends->income, ArrowLeft back to trends,
Enter activates — panel.hidden false, aria-selected "true"). Real Tab-key
walk (page.keyboard.press('Tab'), not .focus()) from page top found both
[data-ins-tab="trends"] and [data-trends-toggle] reachable and keyboard-
operable in BOTH themes, with a visible :focus-visible outline in both:
  light: outline solid 2px rgb(79,70,229)   (+ white 2px box-shadow ring)
  dark:  outline solid 2px rgb(165,180,252) (+ white 2px box-shadow ring)
(Earlier attempt using programmatic .focus()+.click() showed no outline in
dark — traced this to Chromium's :focus-visible heuristic being cleared by
the intervening trusted mouse click on the theme toggle; a real Tab
keypress after the click restores focus-visible as expected. This is a
test-harness artifact, not a page defect — recorded here per the "trace
what you did" instruction, not as a finding.) Focus ring is a pre-existing
site-wide token (BK-run precedent), unaffected by and confirmed intact
after this diff.

